#doc-part([Research and Evidence Synthesis])[
This part provides comprehensive coverage of ME/CFS research, synthesizing findings from clinical trials, observational studies, and experimental research. For each major study, we provide:

- Study design and methodology
- Key findings
- Implications for understanding ME/CFS
- Limitations and caveats
- How findings connect to other research

This synthesis approach makes the scattered research literature more accessible and actionable.

The part concludes with two linked components: the Hypothesis and Speculation Registry (@sec:hypothesis-speculation-registry), which catalogues every hypothesis, speculation, and open question from across the paper into structured, fielded records with explicit certainty scores; and Chapter @ch:proposed-studies, which translates those hypotheses into detailed research protocols. Together they form a bridge from speculative mechanism (developed in depth in Chapter @ch:speculative-hypotheses) to concrete, testable study designs.
] <part:research>
